Upstream NOTICE attributions (Apache License 2.0 section 4(d))
================================================================================

Section 4(d) requires that we reproduce the contents of any NOTICE file
shipped by an Apache-2.0 licensed work we redistribute.

The Apache-2.0 licensed components cls-studio redistributes are:

  python-multipart, fasteners, opencv-python-headless

Optional --with-openvino installs additionally pull these Apache-2.0
packages from PyPI on the user's machine (nothing is bundled):

  openvino, nncf, openvino-telemetry, safetensors, ninja
  (ninja is Apache-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause; packaging, also pulled in, is
   dual Apache-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause and is taken under BSD-2-Clause)

None of these projects publishes a NOTICE file upstream (re-verified
2026-07-29 against each project's repository root — every name in both
lists above). There is therefore nothing to reproduce here. If any
upstream adds a NOTICE file in future, it will be incorporated at the
next dependency refresh.

For the complete list of third-party dependencies and their licenses, see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

