that wheel on the user's own machine.

================================================================================
NVIDIA libraries via PyTorch CUDA wheel (CUDA builds)
================================================================================

The CUDA builds ship the PyTorch CUDA wheel, which transitively bundles
the NVIDIA libraries pinned as nvidia-*-cu12 in
apps/api/requirements.txt, under their respective redistributable
licenses. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md enumerates that pin set; the lockfile
itself is authoritative, and cuSPARSELt in particular carries its own
NVIDIA license terms. cls-studio does not download or package these
libraries from NVIDIA directly; it inherits them from the PyTorch wheel
that PyTorch's maintainers redistribute under the permissions granted by
NVIDIA.

On Linux these arrive as separate nvidia-*-cu12 wheels; on Windows the
equivalent DLLs are bundled inside the torch wheel itself (torch/lib/).

The aggregated obligations text is copied verbatim out of each shipped
wheel's LICENSE / NOTICE / ThirdPartyNotices file into
licenses/third_party/wheels/ at installer build time
(scripts/build_installer.py).

